<title>GREECE: Bank/Greece offers to drain 250 bln drs at 11.90%.</title>
<headline>Bank/Greece offers to drain 250 bln drs at 11.90%.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's central bank offered to drain up to 250 billion drachmas of 14-day funds at 11.90 percent in a fixed rate depo tender on Wednesday, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Payment date is April 2 and maturity value date is April 16, it said.</p>
<p>&quot;In case of oversubscription, bids will be satisfied pro rata, with a minimum allotment of 500 million drachmas,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Bids should be submitted by fax between 1130 local (0830 GMT) and 1230 (0930 GMT).</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
